{"name":"Eye Popping Cherry","hex":"#bb0077","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eye","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An organ through which animals see (“perceive surroundings via light”).","The visual sense."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To carefully or appraisingly observe (someone or something).","To consider."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye"},{"term":"popping","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very lively."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or sound of something that pops.","A style of funk dance involving rapid contractions and relaxations of the muscles to switch between poses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/popping"},{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Popping Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"\"Popping Cherry\" is the third episode of the first season of the American crime drama television series Dexter. The episode was written by co-executive producer Daniel Cerone, and directed by co-executive producer Michael Cuesta. It originally aired on Showtime on October 15, 2006."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/James_Doakes_in_%22Popping_Cherry%22%2C_Dexter_Season_1_Episode_3.png/330px-James_Doakes_in_%22Popping_Cherry%22%2C_Dexter_Season_1_Episode_3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popping_Cherry"},{"title":"Exophthalmos","blocks":[{"text":"Exophthalmos is a bulging of the eye anteriorly out of the orbit. Exophthalmos can be either bilateral or unilateral. Complete or partial dislocation from the orbit is also possible from trauma or swelling of surrounding tissue resulting from trauma."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Girl_aged_17_years_with_marked_proptosis_Wellcome_L0062481.jpg/330px-Girl_aged_17_years_with_marked_proptosis_Wellcome_L0062481.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exophthalmos"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye"},{"title":"Popping","blocks":[{"text":"Popping is a street dance adapted out of the earlier boogaloo cultural movement in Oakland, California. As boogaloo spread, it would be referred to as \"robottin'\" in Richmond, California; Strutting movements in San Francisco and San Jose; and the Strikin' dances of the Oak Park community in Sacramento, and \"Pop-Locking\" of Los Angeles which were popular through the mid-1960s to the late 1970s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Popping.jpg/330px-Popping.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popping"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Casazza_1.jpg/500px-Casazza_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Casazza_1.jpg/500px-Casazza_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Exophthalmos in Acrocephalosyndactyly type 1","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A